OBSERVATIONS (non-blocking, not criteria):
  O1. The comment added to budget_fit.go cites "Ruling 2026-08-29a"; the
      applicable ruling is 2026-08-29b (29a is W4's dead-band). Wrong
      cross-reference in a comment only; no behavioural effect.
  O2. Consequence of choosing the sum identity (as the ruling directs): on a
      fractional-cent base the displayed adjustment is no longer exactly
      displayed-base x (mult-1). Fixture 7386.555: displayed 7386.56 x 0.1 =
      738.656 -> would display 738.66, but the row shows 738.65 so that
      7386.56 + 738.65 = 8125.21 = the displayed total. This is the
      deliberate trade the ruling makes; recorded so the lead knows the
      residual sub-cent artefact exists.
  O3. Unchanged from attempt 1 and previously accepted by this lane: the
      `{{if .SubItems}}` block emits 4 whitespace-only lines for rows
      without sub-items, so rows without SubItems are identical after
      whitespace collapse rather than byte-identical (proved at attempt 1
      by master-vs-branch render comparison; the template diff is
      unchanged in structure at attempt 2).

